Subject: [PATCH] chrome: propagate the device profile to every child process

The profile loader reaches only the browser process without this, which makes it
useless for almost everything it exists to do.

deviceMemory is the worked example. ApproximatedDeviceMemory is a per-process
static computed independently in the browser, for the Device-Memory request
header, and in the renderer, for navigator.deviceMemory. A profile reaching only
one of them makes the header a server receives contradict the value JavaScript
reports — a contradiction trivially checked server-side and invisible from
inside the renderer.

kCommonSwitchNames is copied for every child process type, which is why the
switch belongs there rather than in a per-type list: the GPU process needs the
profile for GPUInfo, the network process for proxy configuration, and any
process type added later gets it without another edit.

Ledger: profile.loader-reach.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index 8436913..5130820 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -2951,6 +2951,15 @@ void ChromeContentBrowserClient::AppendExtraCommandLineSwitches(
   static const char* const kCommonSwitchNames[] = {
       embedder_support::kUserAgent,
       switches::kUserDataDir,  // Make logs go to the right file.
+      // Apostate: the device profile must reach every process type, not just
+      // renderers. deviceMemory is the worked example — it is computed
+      // independently in the browser for the Device-Memory request header and
+      // in the renderer for navigator.deviceMemory, so a profile that reaches
+      // only one of them makes the header contradict JavaScript. GPU and
+      // network processes have their own reasons. This list is copied for every
+      // child, which is why the switch belongs here rather than in a
+      // per-process-type list.
+      ::switches::kApostateProfile,
   };
   command_line->CopySwitchesFrom(browser_command_line, kCommonSwitchNames);
 
